FINAL ANSWER:
**Short answer:** ask Gonzalo Rodriguez, and have Divya Rao review. Both have recent commits. I'd add Hye-jin Park as a second reviewer.

These figures come from `surviving-lines --reviewers lib/rack/attack/store_proxy`, which counts surviving lines with `git blame -w -M -C`. The data is as of 2026-04-14, and I left it unchanged. Nothing was written to `.mailmap`.

**Owners by surviving lines (332 lines counted, all 7 files):**

| Person | Lines | Share | Commits | Last commit | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| hakanensari | 74 | 22.3% | 1 | 2014-04-15 | inactive |
| Gonzalo Rodriguez | 59 | 17.8% | 24 | 2026-03-09 | active |
| Divya Rao | 53 | 16.0% | 1 | 2026-01-28 | active |
| Hye-jin Park | 31 | 9.3% | 2 | 2026-02-20 | active |
| Brad Lindsay | 25 | 7.5% | 1 | 2018-02-06 | inactive |
| 18 more authors | | | | | |

The default table gave no combined share for the 18 other authors. The merged-identity run did not change any top-five figure.

- **hakanensari** has the most lines. They made the first commit on 2014-04-15 and have had no commits in the last year, so they are probably not reachable. Treat them as the original author only.
- **Gonzalo Rodriguez** is the best person to ask. They have 24 commits on this path, and the latest was 2026-03-09.
- **Divya Rao** holds 16.0% of the lines from one commit (2026-01-28) and is active.
- **Hye-jin Park** has 2 commits and is active. Their 31 lines make them the next-best active choice.
- **Bus factor is 3**, measured on this path: the smallest number of authors whose lines together reach 50%. hakanensari, Gonzalo Rodriguez and Divya Rao hold 56.0%. Reaching 80% takes 7 authors.

**What the figures leave out or adjust:**
- **Bots:** I excluded 1 bot identity (14 lines, 1 commit).
- **Reformat commits:** none were set aside.
- **Mechanical rewrites:** I checked and set aside none. One candidate looks mechanical and I kept it: `20d6682` "style: fix Lint/HandleExceptions rubocop" by Gonzalo Rodriguez, 2 surviving lines. It is too small to change the ranking.
- **Moved code:** 37 of 346 lines (10.7%) were written in other paths and moved or copied here. The largest sources are `dalli_proxy.rb`, `store_proxy.rb` and `redis_store_proxy.rb`. The credit goes to the people who wrote them.
- **Copy detection:** the figures use `-w -M -C`. Copy detection moved 31 lines in 3 files between authors. Without it, hakanensari has 55 lines (16.6%) instead of 74 (22.3%). Gonzalo Rodriguez has 52 lines (15.7%) instead of 59 (17.8%). Mei Tanaka has 42 lines (12.7%) instead of 11 (3.3%). Mei Tanaka is not in the top five, but without copy detection they would rank third. If Mei wrote the original Redis or Dalli code, they may be worth asking too.
- **One address, several names:** Gonzalo Rodriguez also appears as "Gonzalo" (same address, 59 lines). madlep also appears as Julian Doherty (madlep) (4 lines). Both are counted as one person.
- **Possible duplicate:** Jonathan del Strother appears under two addresses, `<email redacted>` and `<email redacted>`. The merged total is 19 lines (5.7%), which would place them below Brad Lindsay. This is a strong guess from names and addresses, and only they can confirm it. I did not write `.mailmap`.

**What these numbers don't show:** they say nothing about code quality, review history, design discussions or pairing. Code deleted on purpose counts for nobody. Surviving lines show whose code is still there, not who understands it best.
